From 35eb79466ff179b26ad4cf23bb844d748a540972 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex native diagnostic <noreply@native-diagnostic.invalid>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 01:10:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] power: start native diagnostic HPS with hotplug disabled

The export startup requires CPU0-7 to stay online. Rejecting CPU8/9
does not meet that contract while HPS can still remove A53 cores and
retry the rejected A72 cores.

Start the existing HPS enabled state at zero only for the diagnostic
configuration, before its worker starts. Its existing disabled path
skips hotplug decisions while retaining load collection, periodic PPM
work, client registration and normal restart behavior.

The isolated initramfs does not write the HPS control or request suspend.
This is a native experiment correction, not a general hotplug lock or
an upstream submission; it contains no DCO certification.
---
 .../mediatek/base/power/mt6797/mt_hotplug_strategy_main.c    | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/base/power/mt6797/mt_hotplug_strategy_main.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/base/power/mt6797/mt_hotplug_strategy_main.c
index e7d669e..a51181e 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/base/power/mt6797/mt_hotplug_strategy_main.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/base/power/mt6797/mt_hotplug_strategy_main.c
@@ -100,7 +100,12 @@ hps_ctxt_t hps_ctxt = {
 	.hps_regular_ktime = {0},
 	.hps_hrt_ktime = {0},
 	/* enabled */
+#ifdef CONFIG_MTK_A72_RECOVERY_DISCRIMINATOR
+	/* Keep the boot CPU set while retaining HPS power-management work. */
+	.enabled = 0,
+#else
 	.enabled = 1,
+#endif
 	.suspend_enabled = 1,
 	.cur_dump_enabled = 0,
 	.stats_dump_enabled = 0,
-- 
